From b5faec24ab7e985fd6bfcf64114f3b251b4b489a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:28:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add multi-service transactions: DB schema, RPCs, and New
 Order UI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lets staff attach any number of additional service lines to a single
order (e.g. Wash-Dry-Fold plus Comforter/Special Item) so it stays one
transaction — one payment, one receipt, one status lifecycle, one
loyalty award — instead of requiring a second separate transaction.

- New transaction_service_items table: one row per additional service
  line, with its own service/kg/loads/base amount/add-ons and
  optional per-line detergent/fabric-conditioner usage (null means it
  shares the primary service's wash).
- create_transaction_with_service_items() and
  replace_transaction_service_items() RPCs handle the two-phase
  create/edit dance needed because GCash's "gcash_amount = total_amount"
  and the Base+Add-ons manual-override check are both per-statement
  CHECK constraints that can never be deferred.
- enforce_transaction_shop_preferences() patched (additively, zero
  behavior change with no line items) to fold each line's total into
  that manual-override check.
- Per-line inventory consumption extends the existing order_status
  completion trigger rather than adding a parallel lifecycle.
- New Order form (TransactionForm.tsx) gets a "+ Add Service" editor;
  cash/GCash payment validation and the order total now cover the
  whole order, not just the primary service.

Single-service transactions are untouched: they keep going through
the existing plain insert/update paths.

